 "result": "Rules are deferred while the bundle is built and then replayed onto the app at registration.\n\n**1. Recording (before registration)**: `Bundle.attach_route_rule` in `src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:413`\n- It validates that the endpoint and view names contain no dots.\n- It doesn't touch the app. It calls `self.record(lambda s: s.attach_route_rule(...))`, which appends to `deferred_functions` (`Bundle.record`, L224).\n\n**2. Registration**: `Tessel.register_bundle` (`src/tessel/sansio/app.py:571`) calls `Bundle.register(app, options)` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:273`). That method:\n- builds a `BundleSetupState` via `make_setup_state` (L246);\n- registers the bundle's static route through `state.attach_route_rule` when it has a static folder (L323);\n- merges view functions and handlers via `_merge_bundle_funcs` (L379);\n- runs every recorded callback with `deferred(state)` (L334);\n- recurses into nested bundles, combining their `url_prefix`, `subdomain` and `name_prefix` (L349).\n\n**3. Applying to the app**: `BundleSetupState.attach_route_rule` (`src/tessel/sansio/bundles.py:87`)\n- It prepends `url_prefix` to the rule.\n- It sets the subdomain and merges `url_defaults`.\n- It prefixes the endpoint with `name_prefix.name.`.\n- It then calls `self.app.attach_route_rule(...)`, the app-level method that adds the rule to the `url_map`.",
